Release installer — bundled STT runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The release installer ships the speech-to-text sidecar frozen with PyInstaller
(see docs/adr/0006). It redistributes a CPython runtime (Python Software
Foundation License) and these third-party libraries, each under a permissive
license:

  faster-whisper                        MIT
  CTranslate2                           MIT
  ONNX Runtime                          MIT
  grpcio                                Apache-2.0
  NumPy / tokenizers / huggingface-hub  BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0
  PyAV                                  BSD-3-Clause (bundles FFmpeg shared
                                        libraries, LGPL-2.1-or-later)

The NVIDIA cuBLAS and cuDNN runtime libraries are NOT bundled. On a machine with
an NVIDIA GPU, Lashon downloads them from PyPI on first run, under NVIDIA's own
license terms — the same wheels `pip install` would fetch.
